<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taizhou, Jiangsu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Taizhou is a city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiangsu">Jiangsu</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, on the north bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a>. Its coastal plain was long a centre of salt production, and it was among the salt workers of the area that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhang-shicheng">Zhang Shicheng</a>, a salt boatman, began his revolt against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a> in 1353. The city should not be confused with Taizhou in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhejiang">Zhejiang</a> province.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/taizhou-jiangsu.jpg" alt="Taizhou, Jiangsu" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Leiem · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_from_Qingfengge_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
